     "type": "application",
     "title": "Set Up Your Seminar Toolkit",
     "content": "Before Lesson 2, prepare like a graduate student:\n\n1. **Get the text** — any edition of *The Alchemist* (the 1993 Alan R. Clarke translation is standard for English-language criticism)\n\n2. **Start a reading journal** with three running columns: *Allegory* (what stands for what), *Repetition* (formulas like 'Personal Legend,' 'maktub'), and *Resistance* (moments where you doubt the book's claims)\n\n3. **Mark the structure** — flag the transitions between the six journey stations from this lesson's map\n\n4. **Write your priors** — one paragraph, before close reading begins, on whether you expect to find the book wise, manipulative, or both. In Lesson 10 you'll compare this against your final judgment\n\n5. **Collect one outside voice** — find a single review (positive or negative) and save it for the reception debate",
