     "explanation": "The Alchemist is the textbook case of 'bottom-up canonization': commercial failure (dropped after roughly 900 copies), a second chance from Rocco in Brazil, then the pivotal 1993 English translation, followed by reader word-of-mouth and celebrity endorsement. Crucially, option D inverts reality — elite critics largely scorned the book even as it became the most translated work by a living author. Readers, not the academy, made it a classic.",
