     "explanation": "The scholarly point is rhetorical, not metaphysical: Coelho deliberately positions his own story (institutionalization for wanting to write, the Camino pilgrimage at 39, the book's rejection-to-triumph arc) as evidence for the novel's doctrine. One life cannot 'prove' a universal claim — that's the survivorship-bias problem we'll dissect in Lesson 10. And while some critical schools do bracket biography, the New Critical extreme in option B overstates; here the author's self-presentation is part of the text's reception apparatus and thus fair game for analysis.",
