     "explanation": "The alchemist's prophecy is a slow-corrosion narrative: year one happy, year two haunted by returning omens, years three and four spiritually deaf — with the cruelest consequence that love itself curdles, as Santiago would come to see Fatima as the reason he quit and she would recognize his unhappiness. The argument's force is that it defends leaving *in the name of the love itself*: only a completed Legend protects the relationship from resentment. The alchemist never validates staying — the fable permits no such equivalence.",
