     "explanation": "The genuine debate has two strong poles. The critique: every male character has an independent telos while Fatima's 'dream' is structurally Santiago himself; the proud-waiting-woman ethic is narrated through male needs; the gendered symbol system (man-wind, woman-desert) runs deep. The defense: she makes her choice in articulate direct speech, flat characterization is the fable's universal condition, and she already embodies the non-possessive love the hero must be taught. Removing her would in fact collapse the plot's resolution — her stillness is what lets the circle close.",
