     "explanation": "The alchemist states the rule directly: people seeking only the treasure of their Personal Legend never find it; those who sought only gold failed at the Work because they missed that the metal is the lesser term. The Englishman is the living illustration — ten years of correct information, zero transformation. The metaphor's logic also explains why the alchemist, already master, treats gold-making as nearly trivial. Note option D's trap: the novel distinguishes desiring gold from following a Legend — the merchant who wants only wealth is contrasted with Santiago throughout.",
