     "explanation": "Coelho engineers deniability into his climax: the wind is a real, named storm (weather, says the skeptic), the witnesses are stratified by belief, and the narration stays flat. But the displacement — Santiago standing across the camp when the sand settles — is the one detail no natural reading covers, and the text offers no mover. The construction gives every reader a tenable position while preserving, for those who want it, an irreducible miracle. Recognizing such engineered ambiguity is a core close-reading skill; options A and C invent textual support that does not exist.",
