     "explanation": "The Alchemist's reception is the modern textbook case of the popular/critical split: record-breaking sales, the Guinness translation record, and celebrity adoption ran parallel to elite dismissal — Bloom's verdict, recurring complaints of aphoristic banality and flat characters, and open controversy over Coelho's Academy seat. Crucially for your essays: neither verdict engaged the other's metric (use-value vs. art-value). The scholarly task is not to pick a side reflexively but to be able to argue both languages with textual evidence.",
